            <ArticleTitle>Celiac block for the treatment of pancreatic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>127-33</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Neurolytic celiac plexus block (NCPB) is commonly performed to relieve pancreatic cancer pain. Since Kappis described the percutaneous NCPB, a number of variations of this technique have been proposed to improve analgesic results and minimize complications. In this article, we review and discuss techniques, results, and complications of NCPB.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
